{
  "comment": [
    "Shared host classification vectors for a plain-HTTP Metro server URL.",
    "class: what every classifier returns for this exact host string: metro-url-policy (Rust), classifyHost",
    "(apps/desktop/src/api/serverUrl.ts) and hostClass (crates/server/src/admin_web/admin.js).",
    "installer: what the runner installers (install-metro-runner-linux.sh, metro-runner-container.sh and",
    "metro-runner-container.ps1) do with http://<host>:8787 when it differs from class. They take only the exact",
    "loopback literals localhost, 127.0.0.1 and [::1], and refuse other names for this machine, trailing dots and",
    "malformed hosts. A trailing dot sends the name through the resolver, so 100.64.0.1. and localhost. are other.",
    "Numeric hosts must be a canonical dotted quad: resolvers read 100.077.0.1 as octal (100.63.0.1),",
    "0x64 as hex and 100.64.1 as shorthand, so classifiers never call those Tailscale; installers refuse them.",
    "no_proxy: how ureq 3 (NSH fetch, runners up to 0.4.0) matches a NO_PROXY value against a URI host.",
    "direct_uri_hosts: canonical URI hosts that metro_url_policy::direct_no_proxy_entries() must exempt from proxies.",
    "launcher_no_proxy_entries: exactly metro_url_policy::direct_no_proxy_entries(), which the desktop launcher adds to the UI's NO_PROXY.",
    "Authorities: after an IPv6 literal's ] only :<digits> may follow ([::1]:99] is refused), and names are checked for DNS characters before any shell splitting (*.ts.net, box.. are refused)."
  ],
